-- title:
--   Row-10 reduced product of the Newton approximant and inverse multiplier
-- statement:
--   These are explicit finite coefficient data for the degree-10 inverse cubic of a fifth power of $z^3-z-\beta$. The algebraic parameter used in the later proofs satisfies $\alpha^3=1001/20-66\alpha+21\alpha^2$. This bundle defines the explicit degree-at-most-62 polynomial $V_\alpha(t)$ with rational quadratic coefficient expressions in $\alpha$. The separately proved identity $Q_\alpha(t)P_\alpha(t)=V_\alpha(t)$ is used in the inverse-derivative residual certificate. The table records exact coefficients; it does not assume the product identity.
-- source:
--   https://gist.github.com/Amal-David/adce933460b7501cb123f483f62775eb/f5a76eda649f3e995a8ec6b98387b23b64c6debb#file-fifth-md; H5_COMPLETE_CHAIN.md, Sections 1–4; lower/H5_LOWER_MIDDLE_COMPLETION.md and upper/H5_UPPER_BRIDGE.md in the archived research checkpoint. The finite Newton coefficient arrays are auxiliary exact certificates constructed for the accompanying Lean formalization, and are specified in full by this definition submission.

